Geology — Earth materials, processes, history, and investigation (@geology: 0, is #chapter, #geology "foundations/Reading-geology-from-zero.lingua#r_3H533XF25V4VZX2GZ149Q8M6KQ") { r_3CK43VQS79NK0STWNPSCS8YM06
Begin with a rock, landscape, map, or question about the ground beneath a system. Learn to describe observations, identify materials, read space and time, and test an explanation of how the Earth changed. No previous geology course is assumed; mathematical, chemical, measurement, and computational preparation appears where used.

[Begin geology with sustained reading and a gradual practical progression](foundations/Reading-geology-from-zero.lingua#r_3H533XF25V4VZX2GZ149Q8M6KQ) begins a substantial progression through complete physical/historical geology books, Portuguese regional books, field/laboratory manuals, and university exercises. The later structural, chronological, mapping, reconstruction, and research studies demand advanced practical and academic understanding. A reader can enter at a specific question and return for an unfamiliar foundation.

| Reading area | Records |
| --- | --- |
